course: dictionary
lesson: 5146
title: Iridium and the dinosaurs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Iridium is a very hard, heavy, silvery metal. It is a chemical element with the symbol Ir, and it hardly rusts or wears away. Scientists value it for things that must last a long time, such as spark plugs and pen nibs.
explain: Words around a word give clues. «A thin clay layer rich in iridium marks the end of the dinosaurs.» Rich in means having a lot of something, so this layer contains a lot of iridium. Ask yourself what word would fit, then test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: «Iridium is rare on Earth but common in asteroids.» The word but shows that the two ideas are opposites. Rare means not found often, and common means found a lot, so iridium is hard to find on Earth but plentiful in space rocks.
explain: In 1980 Luis and Walter Alvarez found this clay layer all over the world. Below it there are dinosaur fossils, and above it there are none, apart from birds. Scientists used the iridium layer as a clue to work out, or infer, what happened to the dinosaurs.
fact: Iridium is a chemical element with the symbol Ir.
fact: «Iridium» means a very hard, heavy, silvery metal that hardly rusts or wears away.
fact: An «iridium layer» is a thin layer of clay rich in iridium, found all over the world, laid down about 66 million years ago.
fact: The iridium layer helped scientists infer that a huge asteroid hit the Earth when the dinosaurs died out.
fact: Iridium is used in spark plugs and pen nibs.
exercise: «A thin clay layer rich in iridium marks the end of the dinosaurs.» What does rich in mean here? | Lost from | Made of wood | *Containing a lot of | Shaped like
exercise: «Iridium is rare on Earth but common in asteroids.» What does rare mean? | Found everywhere | *Not found often, hard to find | Very heavy | Very hard
exercise: What is iridium? | A type of cloud | A soft red fruit | A kind of dinosaur | *A very hard, heavy, silvery metal
test: Why is the iridium layer important to scientists? | It is a metal they can use to make a dinosaur | It shows where the birds live | *It helped them infer that a huge asteroid hit the Earth | It is a sort of rock that floats
test: «Below the clay layer there are dinosaur fossils, and above it none, apart from birds.» What does this suggest? | Dinosaurs lived above the layer | Fossils are made of iridium | Birds lived before the dinosaurs | *The dinosaurs died out at about the time of the layer
exam: Which words best describe iridium? | Soft and wet | *Very hard, heavy and silvery | Light and bright red | Hot and liquid
